('IELTS_2','IELTS_2_2365','resolve','rɪ''zɑlv','rɪ''zɒlv','[v] 解决；决定','Barnet was desperate for money to resolve his financial problems.  巴尼特急需钱来解决他的经济问题。'),
('IELTS_2','IELTS_2_2366','resonant','''rɛznənt','''rez(ə)nənt','[adj] 反响的；共鸣的','the violin’s smooth, resonant tone  小提琴圆润悠扬的音色'),
('IELTS_2','IELTS_2_2367','resort','rɪ''zɔrt','rɪ''zɔːt','[vi&n] 求助','His punishing work schedule had made him resort to drugs.  他那累人的工作日程已经使他不得不求助于毒品了。'),
('IELTS_2','IELTS_2_2368','resource','''risɔrs','rɪ''sɔːs; rɪ''zɔːs','[n] 资源；机智','Canada’s vast mineral resources  加拿大丰富的矿产资源'),
('IELTS_2','IELTS_2_2369','respiration',',rɛspə''reʃən','respɪ''reɪʃ(ə)n','[n] 呼吸作用；一次呼吸；植物光合作用','His respiration grew fainter throughout the day.  一天当中，他的呼吸越来越微弱。'),
('IELTS_2','IELTS_2_2370','responsive','rɪ''spɑnsɪv','rɪ''spɒnsɪv','[adj] 易于做出迅速反应的','With an election coming soon, your representative should be very responsive to your request.  大选在即，你们的代表应该对你们的要求作出迅速积极的反应。'),
('IELTS_2','IELTS_2_2371','restless','''rɛstləs','ˈrestləs','[adj] 焦躁不安的','After a few weeks in Marseille, I grew restless and decided to move on.  在马赛住了几星期后，我开始待不住了，决定换个地方。'),
