('IELTS_2','IELTS_2_2896','fundamental',',fʌndə''mɛntl','fʌndə''ment(ə)l','[adj] 基础的；十分重要的; [n] 基本原则','We have to tackle the fundamental cause of the problem.  我们必须解决问题的根本原因。'),
('IELTS_2','IELTS_2_2897','funeral','''fjunərəl','''fjuːn(ə)r(ə)l','[n] 葬礼，丧葬','The funeral will be held at St. Martin’s Church.  葬礼将在圣马丁教堂举行。'),
('IELTS_2','IELTS_2_2898','funnel','''fʌnl','''fʌn(ə)l','[n] 漏斗，烟囱; [v] 汇集','...a ship with three masts and two funnels.  …一艘有3根桅杆和2个烟囱的轮船。'),
('IELTS_2','IELTS_2_2899','furious','''fjʊrɪəs','''fjʊərɪəs','[adj] 狂怒的','She was absolutely furious .  她怒不可遏。'),
('IELTS_2','IELTS_2_2900','furnace','''fɝnɪs','''fɜːnɪs','[n] 炉子，熔炉','We had better fire up the furnace.  我们最好把炉子生起来。'),
('IELTS_2','IELTS_2_2901','furnish','''fɝnɪʃ','''fɜːnɪʃ','[v] 供应，用家具装备房子','Having bought the house, they couldn’t afford to furnish it.  买下房子后，他们没有钱买家具了。'),
('IELTS_2','IELTS_2_2902','fury','''fjʊri','''fjʊərɪ','[n] 狂怒，愤怒的爆发','I was shaking with fury .  我气得发抖。'),
('IELTS_2','IELTS_2_2903','fuse','fjuz','fjuːz','[n] 导火线，引信，保险丝; [v] 熔，烧断电路','two 13 amp fuses  两根13安培的保险丝'),
('IELTS_2','IELTS_2_2904','fusion','''fjʊʒən','''fjuːʒ(ə)n','[n] 熔合，熔接','His previous fusions of jazz, pop and African melodies have proved highly successful.  他先前对爵士乐、流行乐和非洲音乐旋律的融合已经证明是非常成功的。'),
